Assembled by Palestinian[ artist Said] Baalb[aki,] the exhibition presents 50 of Abbo's sketches, etchings and object, as well as texts – all taken from Baalbaki's personal collection of work[ from], and publications[ on, the] elusive sculptor. Baalbaki has[ no work of] his own in this show.
[Born in Saf]ad,[ northern] Palestine, around 1888-1890, Abbo was a farmer and fisherman who later took up carpentry and stone masonry. It was not until he moved[ to] Berlin in 1911 to study sculpture that his artistic career took shape.
